.TH COWFS 4
.SH NAME
cowfs \- a tree whose changes are kept apart
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cowfs
[
.B -D
] [
.B -m
.I mtpt
] [
.B -s
.I srvname
]
.I base
.I shadow
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Cowfs
serves the tree
.IR base ,
with every change to it kept in the directory
.IR shadow ,
so that
.I base
itself does not change.
It posts the service as
.BI /srv/ srvname
and mounts it on
.IR mtpt ;
with neither option, it mounts it on
.I base
in the caller's name space, while its own still sees the real one.
.PP
A file is read from
.I base
until it changes.
An open to write, or with
.BR OTRUNC ,
or a
.IR wstat ,
first copies the file whole into
.IR shadow ,
at the same path, making its directories there as
.I base
has them; from then on the tree has the copy.
A
.I create
is made in
.IR shadow .
A
.I remove
takes the file from
.I shadow
if it is there, and leaves a whiteout for one in
.IR base ,
so the file is gone from the tree but not from
.IR base .
A directory lists the names of both, less the whiteouts, and must be empty in the tree to be
removed.
A rename is a copy under the new name and a whiteout of the old; a directory of
.I base
cannot be renamed.
.PP
The file
.IB shadow /.cow/files
notes each path that was copied or removed, a line each:
.B c
for a copy or
.B w
for a whiteout,
.IR base 's
.B qid.vers
and the SHA-1 of its text when it was noted, in hex
.RB ( -
for a directory), and the path from the tree's root, quoted as
.IR quote (2)
quotes.
A program that later writes the changes back can check by the hash that
.IR base 's
file is still the text the copy began from.
.PP
In the tree,
.B .cow
is a directory that holds only
.BR notes ,
kept as
.IB shadow /.cow/notes\f1;
.IR base 's
own
.B .cow
is not seen, and nothing else may be made there.
.I Cowfs
keeps nothing else of its own: another started on the same
.I base
and
.I shadow
serves the same tree.
.PP
.B -D
prints the 9P messages.
.SH EXAMPLES
A session of
.IR sibyl (1)
serves its project so, for the agent's commands; its review shows
.I shadow
against the real files:
.IP
.EX
cowfs -s sibyl.1.tree /usr/glenda/src/proj /usr/glenda/lib/sibyl/1.tree
.EE
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/cowfs
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sibyl (1),
.IR srvfs (4),
.IR exportfs (4)
.SH BUGS
A copy is of the whole file.
A file opened only to read before another open copies it goes on reading
.IR base .
